-- title:
--   Pinned per-chart addition morphisms lie over Spec R
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring of universe level $u$ which is an integral domain and Noetherian, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $R$ satisfying `W.IsElliptic`. Write $E =$ `projModelCR W.toProjective` for the $\operatorname{Proj}$ of the grading on $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,3)\,R$ modulo the ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of `W.toProjective`, induced by the homogeneous submodules, with structure morphism `projModelStrCR W.toProjective` to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ given by `Proj.toSpecZero` followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra map $R \to$ (degree-zero part), and write $\mathcal{A}_i$ for the degree-zero homogeneous localisation of that graded quotient away from the class of $X_i$. Assume given, for each pair $i,j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, a morphism $\mathrm{pcm}_{ij} \colon \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{A}_i \otimes_R \mathcal{A}_j) \to E$, and assume these are pinned on the six Lange–Ruppert opens: for all $i,j$ and all $l \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, the morphism `kw_lrSixU_locMap W i j l`, namely $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the localisation map of $\mathcal{A}_i \otimes_R \mathcal{A}_j$ away from `kw_lrSixU W i j l`, followed by $\mathrm{pcm}_{ij}$, equals `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l`. Then for every pair $ij \in \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \times \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, the isomorphism `kwProjPullbackChartIsoCR R W.toProjective ij.1 ij.2` from the $ij$-th chart of the pullback open cover of $E \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} E$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{A}_{ij.1} \otimes_R \mathcal{A}_{ij.2})$, followed by $\mathrm{pcm}_{ij}$ and then by the structure morphism, coincides with the cover map $f_{ij}$ followed by `pullback.fst` and then by the structure morphism.
--
--   This is the over-the-base half of the gluing data for the addition morphism on the projective Weierstrass model: the pinned per-chart addition morphisms are morphisms of schemes over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ when read through the nine-chart cover of $E \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} E$. It is used, alongside the overlap-compatibility statement [`WeierstrassProjModel.perChart_addMorphism_pin_outerCompat`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.perChart_addMorphism_pin_outerCompat), by [`WeierstrassProjModel.exists_addMorphism_of_perChart_addMorphism_pin`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.exists_addMorphism_of_perChart_addMorphism_pin) to glue the charts into a global addition morphism, and also in [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_pcmpin_outerCompat_genericPoint_agree`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_pcmpin_outerCompat_genericPoint_agree).
-- source:
